  "name": "l0_entity_visual_state",
  "about": "The entity presentation words (`walks/L0-r021.md`). `CBaseEntity::SetModel` 0x100ad460 (slot 105, reached by `CFuncIllusionary::Spawn` 0x100bf760 for three runtime `func_illusionary`s): `VEngineServer014` slot 20 looks the name up in the model-precache table (-1 absent) and slot 21 types it; a type other than brush (1) prints `Msg(\"Setting CBaseEntity to non-brush model %s\")` -- the empty name too -- with no early return; then `UTIL_SetModel` 0x101cf4a0 (a NULL or empty name returns untouched; else `VModelInfoServer001` slot 12's index through slot 10 into `m_nModelIndex` +0x1a4, the name through slot 212, the model's bounds), then `+0x1b1 = 1`. `CBaseEntity::Hide` 0x1009d2a0 (slot 66; `CNPC_VCamera::Spawn` 0x10368b70 and `CNPC_VZombie::NPCInit` 0x103defc0 call it on themselves): `m_fEffects |= 0x40` (EF_NODRAW) when not script-hidden, `m_fScriptSavedEffects |= 0x40` when it is, then `ForceTransmit` 0x1009d1e0 (`m_flForceTransmitUntil` +0x90 = curtime + 1.0f). `CBaseEntity::Unhide` 0x1009d380 (slot 67; the zombie's crawl-out task 0x14c at 0x103dfdd5): the same bit cleared, no transmit stamp. The `ScriptHide` / `ScriptUnhide` inputs (0x100a8710 / 0x100a8990) save the live word and write 0xe0, then restore it, each with `ForceTransmit` -- so an entity Hide made NODRAW stays NODRAW across the pair. `CBaseEntity::IsViewable` 0x100a9800 (slot 163; the werewolf's NPCThink round robin reaches it): EF_NODRAW -> false; else `IsBSPModel` 0x100b5110 (SOLID_BSP, or SOLID_VPHYSICS over a brush model) picks `m_MoveType != 0`, otherwise `m_nModelIndex != 0`. Reported as `fail`, a word or site payload differs from retail's.",
